# Force LF in the working tree for source files, on every platform.
#
# Why: without this, git on Windows checks these out with CRLF. Several tests
# assert against the literal text of the SQL migrations, and a pattern written
# as `;\n` silently stops matching `;\r\n` — so the same commit could pass on
# Windows and fail in CI (or the reverse) for reasons nothing to do with the
# code. It cost a confusing debugging round; this ends the class of problem.
#
# Binary assets are marked so git never tries to "fix" their line endings.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sql   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf

*.webp  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.zip   binary
